-- title:
--   Integral rescaled exponential under a local Cartier dual
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $\mathcal O$ a commutative ring in which $p$ is a non-zero-divisor, equipped with an $\mathcal O$-algebra structure on $\mathbb Z/p$ whose structure map has kernel exactly $(p)$, and assume $\mathcal O$ is adically complete for $(p)$. Let $F$ be a $d$-dimensional commutative formal group law over $\mathcal O$: a $d$-tuple of power series in variables indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,d\oplus\mathrm{Fin}\,d$ with vanishing constant term, linear coefficients $\delta_{ij}$ in each block, satisfying associativity, and with the block-swap substitution fixing each component. Let $F_p$ be a $d$-tuple with vanishing constant terms such that $\mathrm{coeff}_m(F_{p,i})\cdot p=p^{\deg m}\,\mathrm{coeff}_m(F_i)$ for all $m\neq 0$, and let $\varphi$ be a $d$-tuple in $d$ variables with vanishing constant terms, linear part the identity matrix, and $\varphi\circ F_p=\varphi(\mathrm{inl})+\varphi(\mathrm{inr})$ after substitution. Let $v>0$ and let $R$ be a commutative Hopf $\mathcal O$-algebra, free and finite as an $\mathcal O$-module, with $R$ and $R\otimes_{\mathcal O}R$ adically complete for $(p)$, together with a surjective $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\pi:\mathcal O[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]\to R$ such that each $\pi(X_i)$ lies in the radical of $(p)R$, $\pi$ is given by $(p)$-adic evaluation at the $\pi(X_i)$, $\ker\pi$ is generated by the components of the $p^v$-th iterate $F$-series (defined by $0$ at stage $0$ and $i\mapsto F_i(\text{previous stage},X)$ at each successor stage), and the comultiplication satisfies $\Delta(\pi(X_i))=F_i(\pi(X)\otimes 1,1\otimes\pi(X))$ in the $(p)$-adic sense on $R\otimes_{\mathcal O}R$. Assume finally that the Cartier dual of $\mathbb Z/p\otimes_{\mathcal O}R$ over $\mathbb Z/p$, that is the $\mathbb Z/p$-linear dual with its ring structure, is a local ring. Then there exists a $d$-tuple $\psi$ of power series in $d$ variables over $\mathcal O$ with vanishing constant terms, such that for every $N$ and every $i$ all but finitely many coefficients of $\psi_i$ lie in $(p^N)$, and $\psi\circ\varphi=X=\varphi\circ\psi$ componentwise.
--
--   The tuple $\psi$ is the rescaled exponential inverse to the rescaled logarithm $\varphi$ of the formal group law $F$; the formal two-sided inversion is automatic from the identity linear part, so the content is the $p$-adic null-sequence property of the coefficients, which holds under the unipotence of the mod-$p$ fibre of the $p^v$-torsion Hopf algebra. It supplies the integral logarithm/exponential package used in the deformation-theoretic step [`Deformation.exists_algHom_baseChange_eq_of_forall_map_mem_fontaineKer_of_forall_ker_eq_torsionIdeal_zmodp`](thm.html#Deformation.exists_algHom_baseChange_eq_of_forall_map_mem_fontaineKer_of_forall_ker_eq_torsionIdeal_zmodp).
